820f1b33-0559-4314-a852-1216bcd00aa4	151b7974-14e3-44fe-947d-fc93cd9031f8	2026-04-03 09:00:59.163548+00	This scan reveals a multi-system pattern dominated by infectious burden and digestive-vascular dysfunction. The most striking finding is Streptococcus agalactiae appearing as the top-scoring condition (score 0.002-0.005) across virtually every organ system — respiratory (0.002), digestive (0.003), blood/lymph (0.003), cardiovascular (0.004), nervous (0.005), urogenital (0.005), and core (0.005). This near-universal microbial signature suggests a systemic infectious load that is stressing immune function and driving inflammatory cascades body-wide. Atherosclerosis follows a similar multi-system pattern (scores 0.008-0.026 across endocrine, cardiovascular, urogenital, nervous, digestive, and core systems), pointing to widespread vascular compromise that compounds organ-level dysfunction.\n\nThe root system analysis points to the DIGESTIVE SYSTEM as the primary driver. With 88 conditions and a risk score of 0.522, it harbors the densest pathology including the highest-connectivity conditions in the knowledge graph: fatty hepatosis (K76.0, connectivity 1.00), colitis/enteritis (K52.9, connectivity 0.94), atrophic gastritis (K29.40, connectivity 0.86), and chronic hepatitis (K73.9, connectivity 0.86). The Ultra Micro Scan (score 0.606, highest risk) confirms this with gallbladder dyskinesia (0.072), duodenal dyskinesia (0.076), gastroptosis (0.172), large intestine dyskinesia (0.177), iron deficiency anemia (0.184), and intestinal enterokinase deficiency (0.221) — all pointing to impaired digestive motility, enzyme production, and nutrient absorption. The knowledge graph confirms dense pathway sharing among digestive conditions via gut microbiome regulation, mucosal barrier integrity, and inflammatory response pathways. Colitis is worsening (slope -0.019), reinforcing active digestive deterioration.\n\nThe cascade proceeds: digestive dysfunction (dyskinesia, dysbiosis, mucosal breakdown) → hepatic stress (hepatic fibrosis pathways, bacteroides fragilis in hepatic tissue at 0.060) → impaired detoxification and nutrient processing → vascular degradation (atherosclerosis multi-system, varix dilatation across 4 systems, haemorrhoids at 0.031) → cardiovascular compromise (score 0.530, neurasthenia at 0.036, cardiac arrhythmia worsening) → endocrine dysregulation (hypothyroidism at 0.062, diffuse goiter at 0.068, adrenal vegetative-vascular dystonia at 0.071) → nervous system effects (neurasthenia at 0.039, VVD across 7 organ systems) → osteoskeletal degradation (osteoporosis across 6 systems at 0.048, driven by malabsorption of calcium/vitamin D and endocrine dysfunction). The infectious agents (Streptococcus agalactiae, Staphylococcus aureus, Pseudomonas aeruginosa) exploit the compromised mucosal barriers and immune suppression, creating a self-reinforcing cycle. These represent analytical patterns in scan data, not clinical diagnoses.	[{"organ_system": "Digestive System", "confidence": "high", "reasoning": "Highest condition density (88 conditions), harbors the top-connectivity knowledge graph nodes (K76.0 fatty hepatosis at 1.00, K52.9 colitis at 0.94, K29.40 atrophic gastritis at 0.86, K73.9 chronic hepatitis at 0.86). Ultra Micro Scan confirms motility disorders (gallbladder dyskinesia 0.072, duodenal dyskinesia 0.076, large intestine dyskinesia 0.177), enzyme deficiency (enterokinase 0.221), and downstream iron deficiency anemia (0.184). Multiple shared pathways \\u2014 gut microbiome regulation, mucosal barrier integrity, inflammatory response \\u2014 link digestive conditions to every other affected system. Colitis is actively worsening per temporal trends.", "downstream_effects": ["Blood and Lymph", "Cardiovascular System", "Endocrine System", "Nervous System", "Osteoskeletal System", "Urogenital System"]}, {"organ_system": "Endocrine System", "confidence": "medium", "reasoning": "Hypothyroidism (0.062) and diffuse goiter (0.068) suggest thyroid axis disruption, which regulates metabolic rate, bone turnover, cardiovascular function, and neurological health. Adrenal involvement shown by atherosclerosis in chromophilic cells (0.008), VVD in adrenal (0.071), and hypertension patterns (0.135). Hypothyroidism has 5 comorbid conditions and 3 biological pathways in the KG, making it a high-connectivity amplifier. Endocrine dysfunction likely amplifies digestive and cardiovascular cascades rather than originating them.", "downstream_effects": ["Cardiovascular System", "Osteoskeletal System", "Nervous System", "Blood and Lymph"]}, {"organ_system": "Respiratory System", "confidence": "medium", "reasoning": "Second-highest organ risk score (0.545) with dense microbial colonization: Streptococcus agalactiae (0.002), Pseudomonas aeruginosa (0.030), Staphylococcus aureus (0.032), plus 5 additional bacterial species in bronchial tissue. Multiple bronchiectasis (0.122) suggests structural damage. Bronchial asthma is actively worsening (slope -0.021). Respiratory infection burden likely contributes to systemic immune activation and cardiovascular stress, but appears secondary to digestive root dysfunction given the KG connectivity data.", "downstream_effects": ["Cardiovascular System", "Blood and Lymph", "Immune Function"]}]	[{"chain": ["Digestive dysfunction (dyskinesia, dysbiosis, mucosal breakdown) \\u2192 Hepatic stress (fibrosis, fatty hepatosis) \\u2192 Impaired detoxification/metabolism \\u2192 Vascular degradation (atherosclerosis, varicosities) \\u2192 Cardiovascular compromise"], "mechanism": "Gallbladder and duodenal dyskinesia impair bile flow and digestive motility, promoting bacterial overgrowth and mucosal barrier breakdown. Intestinal permeability allows bacterial translocation to the liver (Bacteroides fragilis detected in hepatic beam tissue at 0.060), driving hepatic inflammation via oxidative stress and NF-kB pathways. Compromised hepatic function impairs lipid metabolism and detoxification, accelerating atherosclerotic plaque formation (detected across 6 organ systems, scores 0.008-0.026). Vascular damage manifests as varix dilatation (4 systems), haemorrhoids (0.031), and downstream cardiovascular pathology including cardiac arrhythmia (worsening, slope -0.029).", "supporting_pathways": ["Hepatic fibrosis", "Oxidative stress response", "Inflammatory response", "Coagulation cascade", "Vascular smooth muscle contraction"], "key_conditions": ["Dyskinesia of Gallbladder", "Dyskinesia duodenal K-CI", "Bacteroides Fragilis", "Fatty Hepatosis", "Periportal Hepatic Fibrosis", "Atherosclerosis", "Varix Dilatation", "Haemorrhoids", "Cardiac Arrhythmia"]}, {"chain": ["Gut mucosal barrier breakdown \\u2192 Systemic immune activation \\u2192 Multi-organ infectious colonization \\u2192 Autoimmune and inflammatory amplification"], "mechanism": "Mucosal barrier integrity pathway is shared across colitis/enteritis, gluten enteropathy, intestinal dysbiosis, and atrophic gastritis (KG data). Barrier compromise allows Streptococcus agalactiae to achieve systemic distribution (detected in 7+ organ systems at critical scores 0.002-0.005). Concurrent Staphylococcus aureus and Pseudomonas aeruginosa colonization in respiratory, digestive, and cardiovascular tissues indicates immune suppression. Autoimmune regulation pathways link atrophic gastritis, colitis, polyarthritis, and prostatitis via NF-kB signaling, explaining the multi-system inflammatory pattern. Prostatitis is actively worsening (slope -0.027).", "supporting_pathways": ["Gut microbiome regulation", "Mucosal barrier integrity", "Inflammatory response", "Autoimmune regulation", "NF-kB signaling"], "key_conditions": ["Streptococcus Agalactiae", "Intestinal Dysbiosis", "Colitis/Enteritis", "Atrophic Gastritis", "Gluten Enteropathy", "Prostatitis", "Polyarthritis", "Staphylococcus Aureus", "Pseudomonas Aeruginosa"]}, {"chain": ["Digestive malabsorption \\u2192 Endocrine dysregulation (thyroid/adrenal) \\u2192 Bone metabolism disruption \\u2192 Osteoskeletal degeneration"], "mechanism": "Intestinal enterokinase deficiency (0.221) and iron deficiency anemia (0.184) in Ultra Micro Scan confirm malabsorption. Impaired absorption of iodine, selenium, and tyrosine contributes to hypothyroidism (0.062) and diffuse goiter (0.068-0.152 across systems). Thyroid hormone deficiency disrupts calcium-phosphorus homeostasis and bone remodeling. Osteoporosis appears across 6 organ systems (score 0.048-0.064), the widest distribution of any skeletal condition. KG confirms shared pathways: bone metabolism, extracellular matrix remodeling, and cartilage degradation link spondylarthrosis (0.122), osteoarthritis (0.136), and Baastrup's disease.", "supporting_pathways": ["Bone metabolism", "Extracellular matrix remodeling", "Cartilage degradation", "Inflammatory response"], "key_conditions": ["Intestinal Enterokinase Deficiency", "Iron Deficiency Anemia", "Hypothyroidism", "Diffuse Goiter", "Osteoporosis", "Spondylarthrosis Deformans", "Osteoarthritis Deformans"]}, {"chain": ["Vascular compromise + Endocrine dysfunction \\u2192 Autonomic nervous system dysregulation \\u2192 Neurasthenia and multi-organ functional impairment"], "mechanism": "Vegetative-vascular dystonia (VVD) appears across 7 organ systems (score 0.051-0.116), indicating pervasive autonomic dysfunction. Atherosclerosis in neurocytes (0.011) and capillaries (0.009) reduces cerebral perfusion. Adrenal stress (VVD in adrenal at 0.071, hypertension at 0.135) disrupts catecholamine regulation. Neurasthenia registers at DNA/RNA level (0.052) and across nervous (0.039), cardiovascular (0.036), and blood/lymph (0.051) systems. This autonomic disruption feeds back to worsen digestive motility (dyskinesia) and cardiovascular rhythm (arrhythmia worsening), creating a self-reinforcing loop.", "supporting_pathways": ["Inflammatory response", "Oxidative stress response", "Vascular smooth muscle contraction"], "key_conditions": ["Vegetative-Vascular Dystonia", "Neurasthenia", "Atherosclerosis", "Idiopathic Hypertension", "Hypotension", "Radiculopathy", "Neuralgia"]}]	[{"pattern_name": "Systemic Streptococcus Agalactiae Colonization", "conditions_involved": ["Streptococcus Agalactiae (respiratory 0.002)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (digestive 0.003)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (blood/lymph 0.003)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (cardiovascular 0.004)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (nervous 0.005)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (urogenital 0.005)", "Streptococcus Agalactiae (core 0.005)"], "shared_pathways": ["Mucosal barrier integrity", "Inflammatory response", "Immune dysregulation"], "clinical_significance": "Near-universal distribution with volatile temporal trend suggests active systemic infection or colonization exploiting compromised immune barriers. This is the single lowest-scoring condition across the scan and likely both a consequence of and contributor to immune suppression.", "severity": "critical"}, {"pattern_name": "Hepato-Digestive Motility-Absorption Collapse", "conditions_involved": ["Dyskinesia of Gallbladder (0.072)", "Dyskinesia duodenal K-CI (0.076)", "Large Intestine Dyskinesia (0.177)", "Gastroptosis (0.172)", "Intestinal Enterokinase Deficiency (0.221)", "Iron Deficiency Anemia (0.184)", "Bacteroides Fragilis in hepatic tissue (0.060)"], "shared_pathways": ["Gut microbiome regulation", "Hepatic fibrosis", "Mucosal barrier integrity", "Oxidative stress response"], "clinical_significance": "Ultra Micro Scan reveals a coordinated breakdown of digestive motility from gallbladder through duodenum to large intestine, with histamine-mediated involvement. Enzyme deficiency and anemia confirm downstream malabsorption. Hepatic bacterial infiltration indicates compromised gut-liver axis. This pattern is the likely origin point for the majority of systemic cascades observed.", "severity": "critical"}, {"pattern_name": "Pan-Vascular Degeneration", "conditions_involved": ["Atherosclerosis (6 systems, scores 0.008-0.026)", "Varix Dilatation (4 systems, score 0.065)", "Haemorrhoids (score 0.031)", "Obliterating Thromboangiitis", "Endarteritis Obliterans", "Trophic Leg Ulcers"], "shared_pathways": ["Coagulation cascade", "Vascular smooth muscle contraction", "Extracellular matrix remodeling", "Inflammatory response"], "clinical_significance": "Atherosclerosis across 6 organ systems with varicose changes in 4 systems indicates generalized vascular wall degradation affecting both arterial and venous circulation. KG confirms haemorrhoids-trophic ulcers and varicose-trophic ulcers share coagulation and vascular pathways. This pattern compounds organ damage from every other cascade chain.", "severity": "critical"}, {"pattern_name": "Thyroid-Bone-Metabolic Axis Disruption", "conditions_involved": ["Hypothyroidism (0.062)", "Diffuse Goiter (0.068-0.152)", "Osteoporosis (6 systems, score 0.048)", "Spondylarthrosis Deformans (0.122)", "Osteoarthritis Deformans (0.136)", "Insulin-dependent Diabetes Mellitus (0.169)"], "shared_pathways": ["Bone metabolism", "Extracellular matrix remodeling", "Cartilage degradation", "Inflammatory response"], "clinical_significance": "Hypothyroidism with goiter suggests active thyroid gland pathology. Osteoporosis across 6 organ systems is the widest skeletal distribution pattern, consistent with metabolic bone disease from combined thyroid dysfunction and nutrient malabsorption. KG confirms spondylarthrosis-osteoarthritis-Baastrup disease share 3-4 pathways each. Diabetes mellitus (4 systems) adds metabolic complexity with 4 biological pathways and 4 comorbidities.", "severity": "high"}, {"pattern_name": "Gut-Immune-Autoimmune Inflammatory Loop", "conditions_involved": ["Colitis/Enteritis (worsening)", "Intestinal Dysbiosis", "Atrophic Gastritis", "Gluten Enteropathy", "Polyarthritis", "Prostatitis (worsening)", "Psoriatic Spondyloarthritis"], "shared_pathways": ["Autoimmune regulation", "NF-kB signaling", "Mucosal barrier integrity", "Gut microbiome regulation", "Inflammatory response"], "clinical_significance": "KG data shows dense pathway sharing: colitis links to prostatitis and polyarthritis via autoimmune regulation and NF-kB signaling; dysbiosis links to colitis and celiac via microbiome and mucosal pathways; atrophic gastritis links to both colitis and celiac via autoimmune and mucosal pathways. Both colitis and prostatitis are worsening temporally, suggesting an active and expanding autoimmune-inflammatory process originating from gut barrier dysfunction.", "severity": "high"}, {"pattern_name": "Respiratory Microbial Burden with Structural Damage", "conditions_involved": ["Streptococcus Agalactiae (0.002)", "Pseudomonas Aeruginosa (0.030)", "Staphylococcus Aureus (0.032)", "Streptococcus Mitis (0.052)", "Klebsiella Pneumoniae (0.065)", "Multiple Bronchiectasis (0.122)", "Bronchial Asthma (worsening)"], "shared_pathways": ["Inflammatory response", "Mucosal barrier integrity"], "clinical_significance": "Six distinct bacterial species colonizing respiratory tissue with bronchiectasis indicating structural airway damage. Bronchial asthma is worsening (slope -0.021), suggesting progressive airway inflammation. This microbial density in the respiratory system mirrors the digestive pattern, consistent with compromised mucosal immunity systemically.", "severity": "high"}]	[{"priority": 1, "focus_area": "Restore digestive motility and gut barrier integrity", "reasoning": "The digestive system is the identified root driver with the highest condition density (88), top KG connectivity scores (fatty hepatosis 1.00, colitis 0.94, atrophic gastritis 0.86), and Ultra Micro Scan confirming coordinated motility failure from gallbladder to large intestine. Addressing the root system first should reduce downstream cascading to liver, vascular, endocrine, and nervous systems. Colitis is actively worsening, making this time-sensitive.", "supported_by": "KG pathways: gut microbiome regulation, mucosal barrier integrity shared across 6 condition pairs. Interventions: Probiotics (supports 9 conditions including colitis, dysbiosis, helminthiasis), Anti-inflammatory diet (addresses 20 conditions), Magnesium (supports dyskinesia, VVD), Omega-3 fatty acids (supports 29 conditions including gallbladder dyskinesia)."}, {"priority": 2, "focus_area": "Address systemic infectious burden with immune support", "reasoning": "Streptococcus agalactiae is the single most critical finding \\u2014 lowest scores across 7+ organ systems with volatile temporal behavior indicating active infection. Staphylococcus aureus and Pseudomonas aeruginosa show concurrent multi-system colonization. Clearing infectious load requires supporting immune function rather than targeting pathogens individually, as the pattern suggests immune compromise secondary to gut barrier breakdown.", "supported_by": "KG pathways: inflammatory response and mucosal barrier integrity link infections to gut dysfunction. Interventions: Zinc (supports 15 conditions including helminthiasis), Vitamin C (supports 15 conditions), Selenium (supports 10 conditions), Vitamin D (supports 25 conditions including immune regulation)."}, {"priority": 3, "focus_area": "Support hepatic function and detoxification", "reasoning": "Bacteroides fragilis detected in hepatic beam tissue (0.060), with KG showing hepatic fibrosis and oxidative stress pathways linking chronic hepatitis (connectivity 0.86), fatty hepatosis (connectivity 1.00), and periportal fibrosis. The liver sits at the junction between digestive root dysfunction and downstream vascular/metabolic effects. Supporting liver function interrupts the cascade from gut to vascular system.", "supported_by": "KG pathways: hepatic fibrosis, oxidative stress response, inflammatory response shared across 3 hepatic condition pairs. Interventions: N-Acetyl Cysteine (supports 8 conditions including fatty hepatosis, cholestatic hepatosis, chronic hepatitis), Milk thistle/silymarin (supports 7 conditions including gallbladder dyskinesia, cholestatic hepatosis), Alcohol reduction (addresses 12 conditions)."}, {"priority": 4, "focus_area": "Evaluate and support thyroid-endocrine axis", "reasoning": "Hypothyroidism (score 0.062, KG: 5 comorbidities, 3 pathways) and diffuse goiter across multiple systems suggest active thyroid pathology that amplifies bone loss, cardiovascular strain, and neurological symptoms. This is a high-leverage intervention point because thyroid function modulates metabolic rate across all systems. Osteoporosis appearing in 6 organ systems may partly resolve with thyroid normalization.", "supported_by": "KG connectivity: hypothyroidism E03.9 has connectivity 0.80 with 5 comorbidities and 9 interventions. Interventions: Selenium (supports thyroid function), Vitamin D (supports 25 conditions including bone metabolism), Omega-3 fatty acids."}, {"priority": 5, "focus_area": "Implement vascular protection and anti-inflammatory lifestyle modifications", "reasoning": "Atherosclerosis across 6 systems and varicosities across 4 systems represent pervasive vascular damage that will worsen without intervention. Cardiac arrhythmia is actively worsening (slope -0.029). While vascular damage is downstream of digestive and endocrine dysfunction, direct vascular support prevents irreversible structural damage while root causes are being addressed.", "supported_by": "KG pathways: coagulation cascade, vascular smooth muscle contraction, extracellular matrix remodeling. Interventions: Aerobic exercise 30 min/day (addresses 19 conditions), Mediterranean diet (addresses 12 conditions), Walking 10,000 steps/day (addresses varicose veins, trophic ulcers, osteoarthritis), Omega-3 fatty acids (supports 29 conditions), Stress reduction/mindfulness (addresses 15 conditions including VVD)."}, {"priority": 6, "focus_area": "Monitor DNA/RNA carcinoma markers and worsening trends", "reasoning": "DNA/RNA system shows multiple carcinoma patterns at moderate scores \\u2014 duodenum carcinoma (0.217), prostate adenocarcinoma (0.221), pancreas adenocarcinoma (0.233), epidermoid carcinoma of pancreas (0.265). While several are improving (epidermoid carcinoma slope +0.105), these warrant monitoring. KG confirms pancreatic-bronchogenic carcinoma share 5 pathways (MAPK, PI3K-Akt, Apoptosis). Neurasthenia at DNA/RNA level (0.052) may reflect stress-mediated epigenetic effects.", "supported_by": "KG pathways: MAPK signaling, PI3K-Akt signaling, Apoptosis, Wnt signaling, p53 signaling across carcinoma pairs. Interventions: Curcumin (supports papillary cancer, related conditions), Selenium (supports carcinoma conditions), Anti-inflammatory diet, Smoking cessation. Note: These are scan data patterns requiring professional evaluation, not diagnoses."}]	llm	claude-opus-4-6[1m]	4646	IMPORTANT DISCLAIMER: MedBed Insight is an analytical exploration tool, not a medical diagnostic device. The information presented here is derived from frequency-based scan data analysis and pattern recognition algorithms. It does NOT constitute medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment recommendations. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional before making any health decisions. The patterns and correlations identified are for informational and exploratory purposes only.	19eced9f-d8be-4db1-aaa6-1e9920f36706	2026-04-03 09:00:59.163548+00	2026-04-03 09:00:59.163548+00
